# Local deny-list for the privacy gate. Copy to denylist.local.txt and edit.
#
# NEVER commit denylist.local.txt -- it is gitignored, because publishing this
# list would publish exactly the names it exists to keep out of the repo.
#
# A match here BLOCKS. Cover: other accounts you operate, employers, clients,
# their domains, and internal system names.
#
# One term per line, case-insensitive substring match.
#
# Two cautions, both learned the hard way:
#
#   Short terms match inside ordinary words. Prefer the longest distinctive form.
#
#   A term that appears in content you deliberately keep will block every commit.
#   This repo keeps ssh Host aliases and includeIf paths containing organisation
#   names, so deny-list the account handles and email domains instead of the bare
#   organisation name.
#
# other-account-handle
# clientname.com
